psf_analysis — attribution and provenance
==========================================

The PSF measurement algorithm implemented in this package (detect well-separated
sub-resolution beads, fit Gaussians per axis, report resolution as
FWHM = 2.3548 * sigma) is a reimplementation of prior open-source work. We
reimplemented rather than copied the source, but the method and design are theirs
and are gratefully credited here:

1. mesoSPIM-PSFanalysis
   https://github.com/mesoSPIM/mesoSPIM-PSFanalysis
   License: MIT
   The light-sheet PSF analysis notebooks that this feature is modeled on.

2. psf (Nick Sofroniew)
   https://github.com/sofroniewn/psf
   License: MIT
   The 2-photon mesoscope PSF package that mesoSPIM-PSFanalysis adapted, and the
   original source of the detect-beads / fit-Gaussian / FWHM approach.

Notable deviation from the reference: mesoSPIM/psf fit a 2-D Gaussian to the
lateral max-projection of each bead. This implementation fits an independent 1-D
Gaussian to a line profile through the bead peak for each of X, Y and Z, keeping
the three axes fully separate — appropriate for the Flamingo system's strongly
anisotropic sampling (coarse Z-step relative to the fine XY pixel).

MIT License text for the referenced projects is reproduced by their respective
repositories; this package is distributed under py2flamingo's own license.
